# While loops

A `while` loop repeats its body as long as its condition is true. If nothing in the body changes the condition, the loop never ends.

```js
let i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
  console.log(i);
  i++;
}
```

## Exercise

Change the loop so it counts down from ten to zero.

# For loops

A `for` loop gathers the initialiser, condition and increment in one line.

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
  console.log(i);
}
```
